----------------------------------------------------------------------
INSTALLATION VIA COMPILATION
----------------------------------------------------------------------

See also: http://pymolwiki.org/index.php/Linux_Install

REQUIREMENTS

    - C++17 compiler (e.g. gcc 8+)
    - CMake (3.15+)
    - Python 3.9+
    - pip (with build submodule <pip install build>; conda's package name is python-build)
    - Pmw (Python Megawidgets) (optional, for legacy GUI/plugins)
      https://github.com/schrodinger/pmw-patched
    - OpenGL
    - GLEW
    - GLUT (freeglut) (optional, enable with PYMOL_GLUT=ON)
    - libpng
    - freetype
    - libxml2 (optional, for COLLADA export, disable with PYMOL_LIBXML=OFF)
    - msgpack-c 2.1.5+ (optional, for fast MMTF loading and export,
        disable with PYMOL_USE_MSGPACKC=no)
    - mmtf-cpp (for fast MMTF export, disable with PYMOL_USE_MSGPACKC=no)
    - PyQt5, PyQt6, PySide2 or PySide6 (optional, will fall back to Tk
        interface if compiled with PYMOL_GLUT=ON)
    - glm
    - catch2 (optional, enable with PYMOL_TESTING=ON)
    - openvr 1.0.x (optional, enable with PYMOL_OPENVR=ON)
    - libnetcdf (optional, disable with PYMOL_VMD_PLUGINS=OFF)

SETUP OPTIONS

    pip install --help

    Build options are passed as CMake defines:
      --config-settings=cmake.define.<NAME>=<VALUE>

    Common options:
      PYMOL_GLUT=ON|OFF
      PYMOL_LIBXML=ON|OFF
      PYMOL_USE_MSGPACKC=c++11|c|guess|no
      PYMOL_TESTING=ON|OFF
      PYMOL_OPENVR=ON|OFF
      PYMOL_VMD_PLUGINS=ON|OFF
      PYMOL_USE_OPENMP=default|yes|no
      PYMOL_USE_VTKM=2.0|2.1|2.2|2.3|no
      PYMOL_PREFIX_PATH=<path1[;path2...]>

    Environment variables:
      PREFIX_PATH   Path-delimited list of paths to search for headers and
                    libraries, e.g. $HOME/mmtf-cpp:$HOME/msgpack-c:/opt/local
      CXX           C++ compiler command
      CC            C compiler command
      CXXFLAGS      C++ compiler flags
      CFLAGS        C compiler and linker flags
      CPPFLAGS      C/C++ preprocessor flags, e.g. -I/tmp/msgpack-c/include
      LDFLAGS       linker flags
      CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL
                    Number of parallel build jobs

INSTALLATION

    Clean build and installation
      pip install .

    Recommended for developers (verbose build output, incremental build,
    and building C++ unit tests)
      pip install --verbose --no-build-isolation \
        --config-settings=cmake.define.PYMOL_TESTING=ON .

    Example with additional feature toggles
      pip install --verbose \
        --config-settings=cmake.define.PYMOL_GLUT=ON \
        --config-settings=cmake.define.PYMOL_LIBXML=OFF .

RUNNING PyMOL

    pymol
    or
    python -m pymol

Good luck!
